@node Migrating from xcape
@appendix Migrating from xcape
@cindex xcape

Escape Pod accepts xcape's mapping string and timeout:

@table @asis
@item @code{xcape -e 'Control_L=Escape'}
@code{escapepod daemon run --map 'Control_L=Escape'}
@item @code{xcape -t 300 -e ...}
Add @code{--tap-timeout 300}.
@item @code{xcape -d}
@code{escapepod event monitor} shows each decision.
@item @code{setxkbmap -option ctrl:nocaps} with @code{xcape -e 'Control_L=Escape'}
One @code{[[dual_role]]} with @code{key = "Caps_Lock"},
@code{hold = "Control_L"} and @code{tap = "Escape"}, which also works on
Wayland and the console.
@end table

Differences: multi-key taps (@samp{A|B}) are refused; the hold key goes down
at once and a tap is added on release, as in xcape; a click between press
and release cancels the tap, which xcape did not do.  On Wayland and the
console Escape Pod works where xcape cannot.
